    "content": "T.I. (Clifford Joseph Harris Jr.), born September 25, 1980, is an American rapper, actor, and entrepreneur from Atlanta, Georgia. Known as a pioneer of trap music, he has earned multiple Grammy Awards and is often referred to as \"the Jay-Z of the South\". He is currently set to retire after his upcoming album, Kill the King.Key Facts & Career HighlightsReal Name: Clifford Joseph Harris Jr.Age: 45 years old (as of Sep 25, 1980)Alternative Name: T.I.P. (\"Tip\")Origin: Atlanta, Georgia (Bankhead)Net Worth: Estimated around $30 millionFilm Roles: Acted in ATL (2006) and American Gangster (2007)Label: Formerly Grand Hustle RecordsReality TV: Starred in T.I. & Tiny: The Family HustleKey DetailsRetirement: T.I. announced at the 2026 Grammy Awards that he will retire from music following his upcoming final album, Kill the King.Business: Beyond music, he is an entrepreneur and author.Legal Issues: T.I. has had several highly publicized legal issues, including a federal weapons charge in 2007 and a 2010 arrest for possession of a controlled substance.Community: Known for his community work in Atlanta, including providing scholarships for single-parent families at Boys and Girls Clubs.Associated EntitiesSpouse: Tameka \"Tiny\" CottleCollaborators: Pharrell Williams, Lil Wayne, Drake, UsherNote: There is also a company called Texas Instruments (TI) and the Therapeutics Initiative (TI), but in the context of entertainment, \"T.I.\" refers to the Atlanta rapper.",
